    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Interoperability",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "قابلية التشغيل البيني",
          "@language": "ar"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Interoperabilidad",
          "@language": "es"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Interopérabilité",
          "@language": "fr"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Интероперабельность",
          "@language": "ru"
        },
        {
          "@value": "互操作性",
          "@language": "zh"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "interoperability",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Interoperability is the standards-based capability of heterogeneous information systems to communicate, exchange data, and use the exchanged information to execute functions effectively.",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "قابلية التشغيل البيني هي القدرة القائمة على المعايير التي تتيح لنظم المعلومات غير المتجانسة التواصل وتبادل البيانات واستخدام المعلومات المتبادلة لأداء الوظائف بفعالية.",
          "@language": "ar"
        },
        {
          "@value": "La interoperabilidad es la capacidad, basada en estándares, de sistemas de información heterogéneos para comunicarse, intercambiar datos y utilizar la información intercambiada para ejecutar funciones de manera eficaz.",
          "@language": "es"
        },
        {
          "@value": "L'interopérabilité est la capacité, fondée sur des normes, de systèmes d'information hétérogènes à communiquer, à échanger des données et à utiliser les informations échangées pour exécuter efficacement des fonctions.",
          "@language": "fr"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Интероперабельность — это основанная на стандартах способность разнородных информационных систем взаимодействовать, обмениваться данными и использовать полученную информацию для эффективного выполнения функций.",
          "@language": "ru"
        },
        {
          "@value": "互操作性是异构信息系统基于标准进行通信、交换数据以及利用所交换的信息有效执行功能的能力。",
          "@language": "zh"
        }
      ],
      "skosxl:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability#label-ar"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability#label-es"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability#label-fr"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability#label-ru"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability#label-zh"
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own glossary wording, verbatim (folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md). Substantive and internal alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#139, smart-ra#140, smart-ra#142): (1) PHC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 9), PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8), and SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-010.md, p. 10): \"Ability of different applications to access, exchange, integrate and use data in a coordinated and consistent manner through the use of shared application interfaces, value sets, concepts and standards, within and across organizational, regional and national boundaries, to provide timely and seamless portability of information and optimize health outcomes.\" (2) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8, citing DIIG): \"The ability of different applications to access, exchange, integrate and use data in a coordinated and consistent manner, through the use of shared application interfaces, value sets, concepts and standards within and across organizational, regional and national boundaries. In the health context, this provides timely, safe and seamless portability of information to help ensure good health outcomes (1).\" (3) PHC handbook §4.4 body (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-023-44-design-system-architecture.md, §4.4, pp. 56-60): \"Interoperability is the ability of different applications to access, exchange, integrate and use data in a coordinated manner through the use of shared application interfaces and standards, which should be defined by the EA and independent of a particular solution’s system architecture (22).\" (4) PHC handbook §4.4.2 body (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-023-44-design-system-architecture.md, pp. 56-60): \"Interoperability is the ability of different applications to access, exchange, integrate and use data in a coordinated manner through the use of shared application interfaces and data representation standards, within and across organizational, regional and national boundaries, to provide timely and seamless portability of information and optimize health outcomes.\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability#label-ar",
      "@type": "skosxl:Label",
      "skosxl:literalForm": {
        "@value": "قابلية التشغيل البيني",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "fa:translationStatus": "unofficial"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/interoperability#label-es",
      "@type": "skosxl:Label",
