        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "The RA draft's own glossary wording, verbatim (folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md); the draft marks this entry [Under review]. Near-identical wording alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#139, smart-ra#142): (1) PHC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11): \"A governed, authoritative and centralized information system that captures, stores and maintains the unique attributes and identifiers of health-care facilities, health service users, products and/or health workforce using a predefined canonical minimum data set.\" (2) SC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"A governed, authoritative and centralized information system that captures, stores and maintains the unique attributes and identifiers of health facilities, health service users, health products and/or the health workforce using a predefined canonical minimum data set.\" (3) PC handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-009.md, p. 9): \"A governed, authoritative and centralized information system that captures, stores, and maintains the unique attributes and identifiers of health facilities, health service users, products and/or health workforce using a predefined canonical minimum data set.\" (4) SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-010.md, p. 10, truncated in source PDF): \"A governed, authoritative and centralized information system that captures, stores and maintains the unique attributes and identifiers of health facilities, health service users, products and/or health workforce using predefined canonical minimum data etc.\" All five are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "skos:editorialNote": "Under review",
      "dcterms:source": "folio/dpi-h-ra/glossary/t-glossary-lead-a31853.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
