    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-story",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "User Story (Requirements)",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "قصة المستخدم (المتطلبات)",
          "@language": "ar"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Historia de usuario (requisitos)",
          "@language": "es"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Récit utilisateur (exigences)",
          "@language": "fr"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Пользовательская история (требования)",
          "@language": "ru"
        },
        {
          "@value": "用户故事（需求）",
          "@language": "zh"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "User Story",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "user story",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Captures a long list of features from an end-user’s perspective. It describes who the end-user is, with their feature wants or needs, and the reason for that want or need (see section 3.2.3).",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "تلتقط قائمة طويلة من الخصائص من منظور المستخدم النهائي. وتصف هوية المستخدم النهائي، والخصائص التي يريدها أو يحتاج إليها، وسبب تلك الرغبة أو الحاجة (انظر القسم 3.2.3).",
          "@language": "ar"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Recoge una lista extensa de características desde la perspectiva de un usuario final. Describe quién es el usuario final, cuáles son las características que desea o necesita y el motivo de ese deseo o necesidad (véase la sección 3.2.3).",
          "@language": "es"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Recense une longue liste de fonctionnalités du point de vue de l'utilisateur final. Il décrit qui est l'utilisateur final, les fonctionnalités qu'il souhaite ou dont il a besoin, et la raison de ce souhait ou de ce besoin (voir la section 3.2.3).",
          "@language": "fr"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Фиксирует подробный перечень свойств с точки зрения конечного пользователя. Описывает, кем является конечный пользователь, какие свойства ему желательны или необходимы, и причину этого желания или потребности (см. раздел 3.2.3).",
          "@language": "ru"
        },
        {
          "@value": "从最终用户的角度记录一长串特性。它描述最终用户是谁、其对特性的需要或需求，以及该需要或需求的原因（见第3.2.3节）。",
          "@language": "zh"
        }
      ],
      "skosxl:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-story#label-ar"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-story#label-es"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-story#label-fr"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-story#label-ru"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/user-story#label-zh"
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 11). Internal and platform alternatives (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) PHC handbook §3.2.3 body (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-013-32-get-to-know-the-users.md, pp. 33-35): \"User stories are the start of generating a long list of requirements, in non-technical terms, that will help the technical team to determine the more specific functional requirements of the system.\" and the template \"“As a… [user persona], I want to… [do what I want to be able to do differently using an electronic system], so that… [reason for wanting that functionality].”\" (2) Platform glossary `user-story` (folio-assistant-core/glossary/cat-harness.glossary.json), which binds the story to a Role rather than a user persona: \"What a reader acting in a Role is trying to do, told as that role: as a <role>, I want <want>, so that <so that>.\" Also used as the functional requirements template (\"As a … / I want … / So that ...\") in SFP handbook §4.5 Table 12 (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-026-45-gather-requirements.md, page-043.md, p. 31).",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
