    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/enabling-environment",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Enabling Environment",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "البيئة التمكينية",
          "@language": "ar"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Entorno propicio",
          "@language": "es"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Environnement favorable",
          "@language": "fr"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Благоприятная среда",
          "@language": "ru"
        },
        {
          "@value": "有利环境",
          "@language": "zh"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "enabling environment",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Attitudes, actions, policies and practices that stimulate and support effective and efficient functioning of organizations, individuals and programmes. The enabling environment includes legal, regulatory and policy frameworks and political, sociocultural, institutional and economic factors (3).",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "المواقف والإجراءات والسياسات والممارسات التي تحفز الأداء الفعال والكفء للمؤسسات والأفراد والبرامج وتدعمه. وتشمل البيئة التمكينية الأطر القانونية والتنظيمية والسياساتية والعوامل السياسية والاجتماعية الثقافية والمؤسسية والاقتصادية (3).",
          "@language": "ar"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Actitudes, acciones, políticas y prácticas que estimulan y apoyan el funcionamiento eficaz y eficiente de las organizaciones, las personas y los programas. El entorno propicio incluye los marcos jurídicos, reglamentarios y normativos, así como factores políticos, socioculturales, institucionales y económicos (3).",
          "@language": "es"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Attitudes, actions, politiques et pratiques qui stimulent et soutiennent le fonctionnement efficace et efficient des organisations, des individus et des programmes. L'environnement favorable comprend les cadres juridiques, réglementaires et politiques ainsi que les facteurs politiques, socioculturels, institutionnels et économiques (3).",
          "@language": "fr"
        },
        {
          "@value": "Установки, действия, политики и практики, которые стимулируют и поддерживают эффективное и результативное функционирование организаций, отдельных лиц и программ. Благоприятная среда включает правовую, нормативную и политическую базу, а также политические, социокультурные, институциональные и экономические факторы (3).",
          "@language": "ru"
        },
        {
          "@value": "激励和支持组织、个人和规划有效且高效运作的态度、行动、政策和做法。有利环境包括法律、监管和政策框架以及政治、社会文化、体制和经济因素 (3)。",
          "@language": "zh"
        }
      ],
      "skosxl:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/enabling-environment#label-ar"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/enabling-environment#label-es"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/enabling-environment#label-fr"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/enabling-environment#label-ru"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/enabling-environment#label-zh"
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "SFP handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, page-009.md, p. 9, citing DIIG), matching DIIG Annex 1.1 Glossary (who-iris/library/9789240010567-eng/sections/page-139.md, p. 127). Shared DIIG Phase 1 concept across DTHs (smart-ra#133 S1, dth-sfp#1 §2.1 Cluster B1); recorded as a candidate.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
